{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusCurvatureCommutator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnusCurvatureCommutator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_commSum_eq_zero_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_commSum_eq_zero_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusCurvatureCommutator.lean#L93-L103","doc":"**The vanishing corollary.** If `ρ` commutes with every generator, the curvature trace is\nzero in every representation. This is the sharp statement of what `(★)` identifies as the source\nof the whole decay object: it is entirely a failure-to-commute effect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_commSum_eq_sum_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_commSum_eq_sum_comm","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusCurvatureCommutator.lean#L81-L91","doc":"**(★) The curvature trace is a commutator-with-`ρ` sum.**\n`tr (ρ · Σ_a [σ_a, σ_{a+1}]) = Σ_a tr ([ρ, σ_a] · σ_{a+1})`, in every representation — no\nBurau, no R-matrix, no family restriction. Sorry-free; the only hypothesis is cyclicity of `tr`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_commutator_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.trace_mul_commutator_eq","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusCurvatureCommutator.lean#L71-L79","doc":"**One commutator, rewritten onto `[ρ, σ_a]`.** For a cyclic linear functional,\n`tr (ρ · [x, y]) = tr ([ρ, x] · y)`. This is the whole content of `(★)`; the sum is a\n`Finset.sum_congr` over it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.commSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.commSum","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusCurvatureCommutator.lean#L65-L69","doc":"The nearest-neighbour commutator sum `Σ_a [σ_a, σ_{a+1}]` — the projector curvature `Ω₂^P`\nwithout its constant `4/[2]_q²` prefactor. Mirrors `MagnusGaugeCurvatureHookColumn.curvatureSum`;\nrestated here so this file stands alone on the cyclicity argument. ","signatureChunk":0}]}